# One topic per chat

Long mixed-topic chats bloat memory, slow responses, and waste tokens.

## When the user message combines two or more unrelated goals

Examples of **separate chats**:
- Scroll-motion fix **and** FAQ copy edit
- Header menu change **and** portfolio page layout
- New home section **and** deploy/CI question
- Feature A implementation **and** unrelated refactor or cleanup

Do **not** start implementing everything silently.

## Required response (before any code changes)

1. **Warn clearly** that the request mixes unrelated topics and will run slower, use more RAM, and grow chat context unnecessarily.
2. **List the distinct topics** you detected (numbered).
3. **Recommend splitting** into separate chats — one topic each.
4. Ask which topic to handle **in this chat now**, or wait for the user to confirm they want everything in one chat anyway.

## Proceed with all topics in one chat only if

- The user explicitly confirms (e.g. "do both here", "keep it in one chat"), **or**
- The topics are genuinely coupled (same files, same feature, or one directly blocks the other).

## Coupled (OK in one chat)

- CSS + JS for the same scroll section
- Astro component + its stylesheet for one section
- Bug fix + small follow-up in the same component the user just mentioned

## Uncoupled (warn and split)

- Two different pages or site sections
- Content/copy + unrelated animation work
- Infrastructure/deploy + UI feature work
